                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The PSA level is significantly elevated above the normal range for females; however, PSA is not typically relevant in women, as it is a marker for prostate tissue. This result may indicate a laboratory or data entry error, or extremely rare ectopic PSA production. Clinical correlation and verification of the test and patient identity are recommended.</td>
